[11/14 17:44:25     11s] @flow 2: # Multi host/cpu attributes
[11/14 17:44:25     11s] @flow 3: #-----------------------------------------------------------------------------
[11/14 17:44:25     11s] @flow 4: # The FLOWTOOL_NUM_CPUS is an environment variable which should be exported by
[11/14 17:44:25     11s] @flow 5: # the specified dist script.  This connects the number of CPUs being reserved
[11/14 17:44:25     11s] @flow 6: # for batch jobs with the current flow scripts.  The LSB_MAX_NUM_PROCESSORS is
[11/14 17:44:25     11s] @flow 7: # a typical environment variable exported by distribution platforms and is
[11/14 17:44:25     11s] @flow 8: # useful for ensuring all interactive jobs are using the reserved amount of CPUs.
[11/14 17:44:25     11s] @flow 9: if {[info exists ::env(FLOWTOOL_NUM_CPUS)]} {
[11/14 17:44:25     11s] @flow 10: set max_cpus $::env(FLOWTOOL_NUM_CPUS)
[11/14 17:44:25     11s] @flow 11: }
[11/14 17:44:25     11s] @flow 17: switch -glob {tempus} {
[11/14 17:44:25     11s] @@flow 0: set_multi_cpu_usage -verbose -local_cpu   $max_cpus
[11/14 17:44:25     11s] **WARN: (PRL-39):	Number of local CPUs specified (16) > Actual number of CPUs in the host (8). The lower value will be used.
[11/14 17:44:25     11s] set_multi_cpu_usage -local_cpu 8
[11/14 17:44:25     11s] @flow 1: if {[get_feature -feature opt_signoff]} {
[11/14 17:44:25     11s] @flow 2: if {[is_flow -inside flow:opt_signoff]} {...}
[11/14 17:44:25     11s] @flow 6: }
